2.3   THE PROVISIONAL PATENT — FILE IMMEDIATELY

⚑   Critical Urgency
The KEYSTONE White Paper published on May 29, 2026 begins a 12-month statutory clock. You have exactly 12 months from first public disclosure to file a US patent application or permanently lose the right. Every day without a filing date is legal exposure.

A Provisional Patent Application (PPA) is a lower-cost first step that establishes your official USPTO filing date and grants 12 months of "Patent Pending" status. It is not examined — it simply holds your place in line under the US first-to-file system (Leahy-Smith America Invents Act, 2013) while the full nonprovisional application is prepared.

